    " A hash table, also known as a hash map, is a data structure that stores data in an organized way, making it easy to retrieve. It uses a hash function to compute an index into an array for quick access to desired data.\n\nImagine you have a large collection of books in a library, and you want to quickly find a specific book. A librarian can help you by looking up the book's title or author in a catalog, which lists all the books in the library. A hash table works in a similar way, but instead of using a catalog, it uses a hash function to find the location of the desired"
